/* eslint-disable no-console */
/**
 * Enterprise-scale demo seed — 150 properties cascading through the real
 * 10-phase pipeline, generated by calling the exact same service functions
 * (`projectService`, `recordService`) the live app itself calls, so every
 * eligibility gate, seq number, activity-log entry and decision-gated
 * stage-completion is produced by the real business logic, not re-implemented.
 *
 * Every generated Project is tagged with a `SEED-` code prefix so it can be
 * identified and removed independently later via destroySeedEnterpriseDemo.js
 * — it never touches Projects you built by hand. Users are upserted by email
 * (idempotent) and are NOT considered disposable — the destroy script leaves
 * them alone.
 *
 * Timestamps: the service layer always stamps `createdAt`/`decidedAt`/etc. as
 * "now". Immediately after each create/decide call this script backdates
 * those fields directly (a plain `updateOne`, bypassing the service) to a
 * date appropriate to the property's own simulated timeline, so a property
 * sitting in "Project Closure" reads as having taken months, not minutes.
 *
 * SAFE-ish by design (purely additive, tagged), but this is a real write to
 * your database and will take several minutes given real DB round-trips per
 * record. Run with a smaller PROPERTY_COUNT first if you want to sanity-check.
 *
 *   node src/seed/seedEnterpriseDemo.js
 *   PROPERTY_COUNT=10 node src/seed/seedEnterpriseDemo.js   # small test run
 */
